  "visualFindings": [
    "RGB correction restores the fish, bicycle, candle, sailboat and several checker interiors that the network erases or merges.",
    "Learning only the palette seeds remains vulnerable to confident wrong paper assignments: the fish is still nearly uniform with both learned-seed variants. RGB clustering recovers its two paper identities.",
    "Foreground probabilities are identical by construction. Handles, hands, neighboring decorations and background patches still leak into the predicted body; the rabbit/bird outline can lose actual paper.",
    "Printed floral/striped paper is still interpreted partly as weaving. Its annotated material error worsens; a two-color palette cannot generally identify sheet identity beneath arbitrary print.",
    "Some checker corners still have tiny gaps or bridges. Partial interior annotations do not certify their connectivity, and metrics at 256 pixels do not establish native-resolution boundaries."
  ],
  "nextStep": "Compare production, frozen-network and RGB-calibrated fields through the actual crop, fitter and editable-export pipeline. Preserve all failures and score derived-mask agreement separately from photographed material identity.",
